# Runs before every `git push`. Pre-push rather than pre-commit on purpose:
# committing should stay cheap so work-in-progress can be saved freely, but
# nothing unformatted or lint-dirty should reach a branch other people pull.
#
# These are the same checks CI runs, so a push that passes here will not fail
# CI on formatting, lint, or types.
#
# Ordered cheapest first, so the most common failure is also the fastest to
# hear about: ~2.7s / ~4.0s / ~3.1s, about ten seconds total.
#
# `typecheck` runs `next typegen` before tsc. A bare tsc reads clean off a
# stale .next and then fails on a clean checkout — which is exactly how the
# LayoutProps error got past a local check and into CI.

yarn format:check
yarn lint
yarn typecheck
